>>
endobj
88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (Every day, payment providers onboard thousands of businesses, enabling them to accept digital payments from customers across the country. From small neighbourhood shops to online service providers, these businesses rely on payment infrastructure to operate, grow and reach new customers.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (However, not every business uses this infrastructure for the purpose it claims to serve. Some merchants may register with legitimate business details but subsequently use their payment accounts to collect money for prohibited activities, including illegal betting. Their registration documents may be authentic, and their transactions may appear legitimate when examined individually.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (For a payment provider, this creates a difficult challenge. How do you determine whether a merchant is operating legitimately when neither its documents nor its individual transactions necessarily reveal the full picture?)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (Identifying suspicious activity is only part of the problem. Businesses evolve, customer behaviour changes, and seasonal demand can significantly alter transaction patterns. Overly aggressive controls risk disrupting genuine businesses, while insufficient scrutiny can allow fraudulent activity to continue undetected.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (Payment providers must therefore find ways to assess merchant legitimacy beyond initial registration, recognise when actual business activity no longer aligns with declared business information, and respond proportionately to potential risks.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 46 0 R
/T (Your Challenge)
/E (Your Challenge)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (How might a payment provider identify and address merchants whose actual activities may differ from their declared business purpose, while protecting legitimate businesses from unnecessary scrutiny, disruption or penalties?)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
